      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The executive summary should present the debate as a clash between the urgency of climate action and the immediate risks of economic disruption. Proponents of a rapid phase-out argue that delaying action will lead to catastrophic climate tipping points that no amount of economic growth can fix, while opponents contend that accelerating the transition without adequate safeguards could trigger energy crises, inflation, and severe hardship for low-income households. The core tension lies in balancing the long-term necessity of decarbonization against the short-term reality of energy security and affordability. Ultimately, the report must highlight that the debate isn't just about environmental goals, but about who bears the cost of the transition and whether society can afford to wait.",
      "source": "target",
