      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a bit better. but honestly, even in that version, it feels like the climate side is framed as the \"necessity\" while the economic side is just a \"risk.\" some people would say the economic instability isn't just a \"risk\" to be balanced, but a certain consequence that would cause massive suffering and political unrest. do u think it's even possible to weigh those two things fairly, or is the climate argument always going to carry more moral weight in these types of reports?",
